{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1  \nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS OVERSIMPLIFIED TO THE POINT OF DANGEROUS AMBIGUITY. IT IMPLIES A CLEAR, OBJECTIVE MEANS OF DETERMINING WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, YET OFFERS NO CRITERIA, FRAMEWORK, OR PROCEDURE FOR SUCH JUDGMENT. THIS LEAVES THE DECISION TO INDIVIDUAL SUBJECTIVITY, WHICH CAN LEAD TO CHAOS, ANARCHY, OR TYRANNY OF THE MAJORITY—DEPENDING ON WHO DECIDES WHAT IS \"BAD.\" HISTORY SHOWS THAT MANY UNJUST LAWS WERE ONCE WIDELY ACCEPTED, WHILE MANY LAWS NOW CONSIDERED JUST WERE ONCE DEEMED UNACCEPTABLE. THE SENTENCE IGNORES THE COMPLEXITY OF LEGAL SYSTEMS, THE ROLE OF CIVIC DISOBEDIENCE, AND THE NEED FOR STRUCTURED REFORM VERSUS UNILATERAL REJECTION.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2  \nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE UNDERMINES THE FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLE OF THE RULE OF LAW, WHICH REQUIRES THAT ALL INDIVIDUALS, INCLUDING THE POWERFUL, ARE SUBJECT TO LAWS THAT ARE PUBLICLY ENACTED AND CONSISTENTLY APPLIED. IF EVERY PERSON CAN CHOOSE TO DISREGARD LAWS THEY PERSONALLY DISLIKE, THE VERY STRUCTURE OF SOCIETY BECOMES UNSTABLE. EVEN BAD LAWS CAN BE CHALLENGED THROUGH LEGAL CHANNELS—APPEALS, LEGISLATIVE REFORM, OR JUDICIAL REVIEW—AND THESE INSTITUTIONS EXIST TO PREVENT THE KIND OF ARBITRARY DISOBEDIENCE THE SENTENCE ENCOURAGES. BY REDUCING ETHICAL AND LEGAL DECISIONS TO A PERSONAL MORAL DECISION, THE SENTENCE DISRESPECTS THE COLLECTIVE PROCESS THAT GIVES LAWS THEIR LEGITIMACY AND POTENTIAL FOR IMPROVEMENT.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -1.6093124941107817e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.1576648578047752e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.0059441933408379555}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.007676506415009499}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.016198454424738884}, {"